{{also|Sterben}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|sterben}}, from {{inh|de|goh|sterban}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*sterbaną}}, itself either from {{der|de|ine-pro|*(s)terp-|t=to lose force; lose sensibility, become numb; be dead, be motionless}} or from {{der|de|ine-pro|*sterbʰ-|t=to be stiff, become stiff}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|sterven}}, {{cog|nds|starven}}, {{m|nds|stiärven}}, {{m|nds|sterven}}, {{m|nds|staarven}}, {{cog|fy|stjerre}}, {{cog|en|starve}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃtɛrbən/|[ˈʃtɛʁ.bm̩]|[ˈʃtɛɐ̯-]|[-bən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-sterben.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-sterben2.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-sterben3.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-sterben.ogg|a=Austria}}
* {{rhyme|de|ɛʁbn̩|s=2}}
* {{hyph|de|ster|ben}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|sterben<stirbt#starb,gestorben,stürbe.sein>}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[die]]
#: {{uxi|de|Mein Hund ist '''gestorben'''.|My dog has '''died'''.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|or|intransitive}} to [[die]] {{+obj|de|acc/gen<a (particular kind of) death>}}
#: {{uxi|de|Das Opfer ist einen schrecklichen Tod '''gestorben'''.|t=-}}
#: {{ux|de|Das Opfer ist eines schrecklichen Todes '''gestorben'''.|The victim '''died''' a terrible death.}}

